<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leabua Jonathan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1987</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leabua Jonathan was the first prime minister of Lesotho, leading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basotho-national-party">Basotho National Party</a> from independence in 1966. When he was losing the 1970 election he annulled it, suspended the constitution and ruled by decree, sidelining King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-ii">Moshoeshoe II</a>. His later quarrels with apartheid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> led to a border <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a>, and he was overthrown in a military coup in January 1986.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leabua-jonathan.jpg" alt="Leabua Jonathan" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joost Evers / Anefo · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minister-president_Jonathan_van_Lesotho_(1970).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
